 - observed lines: `2156, 2157, 2159, 2162, 2166`\n  - trace activity: 7 events, 1 calls, 5 line events, 1 returns, 0 exceptions, max depth 3\n  - sample executed lines:\n    - `line 2156`: `if isinstance(values, np.ndarray):`\n    - `line 2157`: `values = ensure_wrapped_if_datetimelike(values)`\n    - `line 2159`: `if issubclass(values.dtype.type, str):`\n- artifact: `pandas/core/construction.py:_sanitize_ndim`\n  - module: `pandas.core.construction`\n  - definition: `lines 695-731`\n  - first observed in trace A: `line 706`\n  - observed lines: `706, 709, 711, 731`\n  - trace activity: 6 events, 1 calls, 4 line events, 1 returns, 0 exceptions, max depth 3\n  - sample executed lines:\n    - `line 706`: `if getattr(result, \"ndim\", 0) == 0:`\n    - `line 709`: `if result.ndim == 1:`\n    - `line 711`: `result = _maybe_repeat(result, index)`\n- artifact: `pandas/core/construction.py:ensure_wrapped_if_datetimelike`\n  - module: `pandas.core.construction`\n  - definition: `lines 490-507`\n  - first observed in trace A: `line 494`\n  - observed lines: `494, 495, 501, 507`\n  - trace activity: 6 events, 1 calls, 4 line events, 1 returns, 0 exceptions, max depth 4\n  - sample executed lines:\n    - `line 494`: `if isinstance(arr, np.ndarray):`\n    - `line 495`: `if arr.dtype.kind == \"M\":`\n    - `line 501`: `elif arr.dtype.kind == \"m\":`\n- artifact: `pandas/core/dtypes/common.py:<genexpr>`\n  - module: `pandas.core.dtypes.common`\n  - first observed in trace A: `line 1776`\n  - observed lines: `1776`\n  - trace activity: 6 events, 2 calls, 2 line events, 2 returns, 0 exceptions, max depth 5\n  - sample executed lines:\n    - `line 1776`: `if not all(is_hashable(arg) for arg in args):`\n- artifact: `pandas/core/internals/managers.py:BaseBlockManager._validate_set_axis`\n  - module: `pandas.core.internals.managers`\n  - definition: `lines 275-289`\n  - first observed in trace A: `line 277`\n  - observed lines: `277, 278, 280, 285`\n  - trace activity: 6 events, 1 calls, 4 line events, 1 returns, 0 exceptions, max depth 4\n  - sample executed lines:\n    - `line 277`: `old_len = len(self.axes[axis])`\n    - `line 278`: `new_len = len(new_labels)`\n    - `line 280`: `if axis == 1 and len(self.items) == 0:`\n- Additional artifact candidates omitted: `22`"}, {"content": "Let's start by focusing on the specific part of the feature description that mentions the change needed in the code. The description suggests modifying the error message in the `StringMethods._validate` method within the `pandas/core/strings/accessor.py` file.\n\nWe'll first check this file and then cross-reference with the unique artifacts provided to ensure we cover all relevant areas.\n\n<function=search_code_snippets>\n<parameter=search_terms>\n[\"StringMethods._validate\", \"AttributeError\"]\n</parameter>\n<parameter=file_path_or_pattern>\npandas/core/strings/accessor.py\n</parameter>\n", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "toolu_01", "name": "search_code_snippets", "content": "OBSERVATION:\n##Searching for term \"StringMethods._validate\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound function `pandas/core/strings/accessor.py:StringMethods._validate`.\nSource: Match found for entity name `_validate`.\n```\n221 | def _validate(data):\n222 |         \"\"\"\n223 |         Auxiliary function for StringMethods, infers and checks dtype of data.\n224 | \n225 |         This is a \"first line of defence\" at the creation of the StringMethods-\n226 |         object, and just checks that the dtype is in the\n227 |         *union* of the allowed types over all string methods below; this\n228 |         restriction is then refined on a per-method basis using the decorator\n229 |         @forbid_nonstring_types (more info in the corresponding docstring).\n230 | \n231 |         This really should exclude all series/index with any non-string values,\n232 |         but that isn't practical for performance reasons until we have a str\n233 |         dtype (GH 9343 / 13877)\n234 | \n235 |         Parameters\n236 |         ----------\n237 |         data : The content of the Series\n238 | \n239 |         Returns\n240 |         -------\n241 |         dtype : inferred dtype of data\n242 |         \"\"\"\n243 |         if isinstance(data, ABCMultiIndex):\n244 |             raise AttributeError(\n245 |                 \"Can only use .str accessor with Index, not MultiIndex\"\n246 |             )\n247 | \n248 |         # see _libs/lib.pyx for list of inferred types\n249 |         allowed_types = [\"string\", \"empty\", \"bytes\", \"mixed\", \"mixed-integer\"]\n250 | \n251 |         data = extract_array(data)\n252 | \n253 |         values = getattr(data, \"categories\", data)  # categorical / normal\n254 | \n255 |         inferred_dtype = lib.infer_dtype(values, skipna=True)\n256 | \n257 |         if inferred_dtype not in allowed_types:\n258 |             raise AttributeError(\"Can only use .str accessor with string values!\")\n259 |         return inferred_dtype\n```\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"AttributeError\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound class `pandas/errors/__init__.py:AttributeConflictWarning`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n648 | class AttributeConflictWarning(Warning):\n649 |     \"\"\"\n650 |     Warning raised when index attributes conflict when using HDFStore.\n651 | \n652 |     Occurs when attempting to append an index with a different\n653 |     name than the existing index on an HDFStore or attempting to append an index with a\n654 |     different frequency than the existing index on an HDFStore.\n655 | \n656 |     Examples\n657 |     --------\n658 |     >>> idx1 = pd.Index([\"a\", \"b\"], name=\"name1\")\n659 |     >>> df1 = pd.DataFrame([[1, 2], [3, 4]], index=idx1)\n660 |     >>> df1.to_hdf(\"file\", \"data\", \"w\", append=True)  # doctest: +SKIP\n661 |     >>> idx2 = pd.Index([\"c\", \"d\"], name=\"name2\")\n662 |     >>> df2 = pd.DataFrame([[5, 6], [7, 8]], index=idx2)\n663 |     >>> df2.to_hdf(\"file\", \"data\", \"a\", append=True)  # doctest: +SKIP\n664 |     AttributeConflictWarning: the [index_name] attribute of the existing index is\n665 |     [name1] which conflicts with the new [name2]...\n666 |     \"\"\"\n```\n\nFound class `pandas/core/base.py:NoNewAttributesMixin`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n137 | class NoNewAttributesMixin:\n138 |     \"\"\"\n139 |     Mixin which prevents adding new attributes.\n140 | \n141 |     Prevents additional attributes via xxx.attribute = \"something\" after a\n142 |     call to `self.__freeze()`. Mainly used to prevent the user from using\n143 |     wrong attributes on an accessor (`Series.cat/.str/.dt`).\n144 | \n145 |     If you really want to add a new attribute at a later time, you need to use\n146 |     `object.__setattr__(self, key, value)`.\n147 |     \"\"\"\n148 | \n149 |     def _freeze(self) -> None:\n150 |         \"\"\"\n151 |         Prevents setting additional attributes.\n152 |         \"\"\"\n153 |         object.__setattr__(self, \"__frozen\", True)\n154 | \n155 |     # prevent adding any attribute via s.xxx.new_attribute = ...\n156 |     def __setattr__(self, key: str, value) -> None:\n157 |         # _cache is used by a decorator\n158 |         # We need to check both 1.) cls.__dict__ and 2.) getattr(self, key)\n159 |         # because\n160 |         # 1.) getattr is false for attributes that raise errors\n161 |         # 2.) cls.__dict__ doesn't traverse into base classes\n162 |         if getattr(self, \"__frozen\", False) and not (\n163 |             key == \"_cache\"\n164 |             or key in type(self).__dict__\n165 |             or getattr(self, key, None) is not None\n166 |         ):\n167 |             raise AttributeError(f\"You cannot add any new attribute '{key}'\")\n168 |         object.__setattr__(self, key, value)\n```\n\nFound class `asv_bench/benchmarks/groupby.py:DateAttributes`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n241 | class DateAttributes:\n242 |     def setup(self):\n243 |         rng = date_range(\"1/1/2000\", \"12/31/2005\", freq=\"h\")\n244 |         self.year, self.month, self.day = rng.year, rng.month, rng.day\n245 |         self.ts = Series(np.random.randn(len(rng)), index=rng)\n246 | \n247 |     def time_len_groupby_object(self):\n248 |         len(self.ts.groupby([self.year, self.month, self.day]))\n```\n"}, {"content": "Based on the search results, the relevant function to modify is `StringMethods._validate` in `pandas/core/strings/accessor.py`. Specifically, we need to look at line 258 where the `AttributeError` is raised.\n\nLet's confirm and include this in our final output. We'll also consider the other unique artifacts mentioned in the context to ensure we cover all potentially relevant areas.\n\n<function=get_entity_contents>\n<parameter=entity_names>\n[\n    \"pandas/core/strings/accessor.py:StringMethods._validate\",\n    \"pandas/core/generic.py:NDFrame.__getattr__\",\n    \"pandas/core/accessor.py:Accessor.__get__\",\n    \"pandas/core/construction.py:sanitize_array\",\n    \"pandas/core/dtypes/generic.py:create_pandas_abc_type._check\"\n]\n</parameter>\n", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "toolu_01", "name": "get_entity_contents", "content": "OBSERVATION:\n##Searching for entity `pandas/core/strings/accessor.py:StringMethods._validate`...\n### Search Result:\nFound function `pandas/core/strings/accessor.py:StringMethods._validate`.\nSource: Exact match found for entity name `pandas/core/strings/accessor.py:StringMethods._validate`.\n```\n221 | def _validate(data):\n222 |         \"\"\"\n223 |         Auxiliary function for StringMethods, infers and checks dtype of data.\n224 | \n225 |         This is a \"first line of defence\" at the creation of the StringMethods-\n226 |         object, and just checks that the dtype is in the\n227 |         *union* of the allowed types over all string methods below; this\n228 |         restriction is then refined on a per-method basis using the decorator\n229 |         @forbid_nonstring_types (more info in the corresponding docstring).\n230 | \n231 |         This really should exclude all series/index with any non-string values,\n232 |         but that isn't practical for performance reasons until we have a str\n233 |         dtype (GH 9343 / 13877)\n234 | \n235 |         Parameters\n236 |         ----------\n237 |         data : The content of the Series\n238 | \n239 |         Returns\n240 |         -------\n241 |         dtype : inferred dtype of data\n242 |         \"\"\"\n243 |         if isinstance(data, ABCMultiIndex):\n244 |             raise AttributeError(\n245 |                 \"Can only use .str accessor with Index, not MultiIndex\"\n246 |             )\n247 | \n248 |         # see _libs/lib.pyx for list of inferred types\n249 |         allowed_types = [\"string\", \"empty\", \"bytes\", \"mixed\", \"mixed-integer\"]\n250 | \n251 |         data = extract_array(data)\n252 | \n253 |         values = getattr(data, \"categories\", data)  # categorical / normal\n254 | \n255 |         inferred_dtype = lib.infer_dtype(values, skipna=True)\n256 | \n257 |         if inferred_dtype not in allowed_types:\n258 |             raise AttributeError(\"Can only use .str accessor with string values!\")\n259 |         return inferred_dtype\n```\n\n\n##Searching for entity `pandas/core/generic.py:NDFrame.__getattr__`...\n### Search Result:\nFound function `pandas/core/generic.py:NDFrame.__getattr__`.\nSource: Exact match found for entity name `pandas/core/generic.py:NDFrame.__getattr__`.\n```\n6056 | def __getattr__(self, name: str):\n6057 |         \"\"\"\n6058 |         After regular attribute access, try looking up the name\n6059 |         This allows simpler access to columns for interactive use.\n6060 |         \"\"\"\n6061 |         # Note: obj.x will always call obj.__getattribut