y related to rounding operations on datetime-like data.\n\n<function=get_entity_contents>\n<parameter=entity_names>['pandas/core/arrays/datetimelike.py:TimelikeOps._round']</parameter>\n", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "toolu_01", "name": "get_entity_contents", "content": "OBSERVATION:\n##Searching for entity `pandas/core/arrays/datetimelike.py:TimelikeOps._round`...\n### Search Result:\nFound function `pandas/core/arrays/datetimelike.py:TimelikeOps._round`.\nSource: Exact match found for entity name `pandas/core/arrays/datetimelike.py:TimelikeOps._round`.\n```\n2160 | def _round(self, freq, mode, ambiguous, nonexistent):\n2161 |         # round the local times\n2162 |         if isinstance(self.dtype, DatetimeTZDtype):\n2163 |             # operate on naive timestamps, then convert back to aware\n2164 |             self = cast(\"DatetimeArray\", self)\n2165 |             naive = self.tz_localize(None)\n2166 |             result = naive._round(freq, mode, ambiguous, nonexistent)\n2167 |             return result.tz_localize(\n2168 |                 self.tz, ambiguous=ambiguous, nonexistent=nonexistent\n2169 |             )\n2170 | \n2171 |         values = self.view(\"i8\")\n2172 |         values = cast(np.ndarray, values)\n2173 |         nanos = get_unit_for_round(freq, self._creso)\n2174 |         if nanos == 0:\n2175 |             # GH 52761\n2176 |             return self.copy()\n2177 |         result_i8 = round_nsint64(values, mode, nanos)\n2178 |         result = self._maybe_mask_results(result_i8, fill_value=iNaT)\n2179 |         result = result.view(self._ndarray.dtype)\n2180 |         return self._simple_new(result, dtype=self.dtype)\n```\n"}, {"content": "Next, let's examine the `Properties._delegate_method` in `pandas/core/indexes/accessors.py` to see how the `round` method might be invoked or handled for datetime properties.\n\n<function=get_entity_contents>\n<parameter=entity_names>['pa